course: dictionary
lesson: 12833
title: Enactment: law or acting?
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Enactment is a noun, so it names a thing or an event. It has two main meanings. In law, the enactment of a bill is the moment it is passed and made into law. «The enactment of the new road safety law took effect in May.» The clue words are law and took effect, so this meaning is about rules.
explain: The second meaning is acting out. «Our class held an enactment of the Great Fire of London.» Here the clue is held and the story of a fire, so people are performing a past event. A re-enactment is a kind of enactment that copies something from history, like a battle.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the words around it and then swap your meaning into the sentence. Does «the act of making a bill into law» fit? Or does «acting out an event» fit better? The clues always show which one the writer means.
fact: Enactment is a noun, so it is a thing or an event.
fact: «Enactment» (law) means the act of making a bill into law, or the law itself.
fact: «Enactment» (acting) means acting out a story or event.
fact: A «re-enactment» is an enactment of something that happened in the past, like a battle.
fact: Context clues such as law, parliament or history show which meaning the writer means.
exercise: «The enactment of the new law came after parliament voted for it.» What does enactment mean here? | A small party in the hall | A map of the country | A kind of weather | *The act of making a bill into law
exercise: «Our class held a historical re-enactment of the Romans arriving in Britain.» What is a re-enactment? | A book about the future | A type of weather | *Acting out a past event
exercise: «The children enacted the story of the three bears on stage.» What does enacted mean here? | *Acted out | Painted | Read silently | Forgotten
test: «Parliament passed the bill, and its enactment made it law.» What does enactment mean? | Telling a joke | Losing a document | *The act of making the bill into law | Drawing a picture of parliament
test: «The drama club's enactment of the old tale was loud and funny.» What does enactment mean? | A school report | A list of names | A loud noise from a machine | *Acting out a scene
exam: Which word best fits when a bill becomes law? | Sleeping | *Passing | Painting | Cooking
